WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.000
Facebook founder, Mark Zuckerberg imploded
recently when he was questioned by Congresswoman

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.660
Alexandria Castillio courts has a few weeks
ago we covered it for you and it's getting

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:38.070
worse because we learned not long ago that
Donald Trump and Mark Zuckerberg had a meeting.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.660
Now it was initially a secret meeting in the
sense that it didn't appear on Donald Trump's

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.260
schedule anywhere.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.610
Facebook didn't report that this meeting between
Trump and Zuckerberg had taken place.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:53.670
Eventually news of the meeting did surface
thanks to N a an NBC news report and of course

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.520
only then did Facebook say, well yeah, we
did actually have that meeting and it was

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.690
actually back in October when Zuckerberg had
that terrible appearance before Congress.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:07.150
So Mark Zuckerberg appears on CBS this morning
yesterday and is interviewed by Gail King

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:14.060
and Gayle King asks him about the meeting
and Zuckerberg devolves into just meaningless

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.060
stuttering.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.229
Visibly uncomfortable.

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:17.430
It is not good.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.450
It is not good.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.450
Take a look.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.039
You were in DC recently there, it was reported
later that you had dinner with the president

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:24.039
of the white house.

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:25.090
What was the nature of the meeting?

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.090
Can you say?

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.090
Uh, sure.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:32.960
I mean, we talked about, um, uh, a number
of things that were, that were on his mind

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.890
and, um, and some of the topics that you'd
read about in the news around, around, um,

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:37.890
our work,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.659
we talked about a number of things and topics
in the news.

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:42.189
Super clear, Mark, crystal clear.

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:43.979
I, I totally understand it.

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:47.990
And she tried to follow up on the question
and it actually gets even worse.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:49.799
People would say the optics weren't good.

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:52.060
Did he try to lobby you in any way?

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.060
No.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.960
I mean, I don't think that that's that I think
some of the stuff that people talk about or

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.390
think gets discussed in these discussions
are not really how, okay.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.390
How that works.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.460
I also want to respect that it was a private,
dedicated Brendan's prior discussion.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.460
Did

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.460
he lobby you?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.460
Uh, no.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:14.520
Um, some stuff people talk about things that,
uh, you know, it's not always as discussed,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.520
so I get it.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.160
It was a private meeting.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.760
That's not a defense though.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.980
That's actually part of the problem as I see
it.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:25.780
Donald Trump has publicly talking about Facebook
should do this, Facebook should do that.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.390
Facebook should not do this other thing.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:32.420
Zuckerberg testifies before Congress on exactly
the same issues.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:38.430
It's a train wreck that gives off vibes that
this is truly a terribly bad faith actor.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.669
They keep the meeting, not just private but
secret.

00:02:42.669 --> 00:02:43.980
They're outed.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.860
And then he says a meaningless word salad
and says, you know, it was a private meeting.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.530
Anyway, so I have to be careful.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.530
Now.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:58.480
I do actually think that Donald Trump and
Zuckerberg probably, uh, did not plan nefarious

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.980
things in the meeting.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.320
Don't think it's that explicit.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.830
I mean, they may be nefarious in some ways,
but if you're imagining this cartoonish secret

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.200
meeting where they're whispering about all
of the nefarious things they're going to do

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.199
on Facebook to help Donald Trump there, I
don't think that anything that cartoonish

00:03:14.199 --> 00:03:15.980
or dramatic took place.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.760
This is just how the hubs of power continue
chugging along.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.000
Peter teal was also at the meeting, which
only raises even more red flags.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.870
That's a story for another day.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.540
If you don't know who Peter teal is, I envy
you.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.010
Uh, that, that's great.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:36.850
Uh, now let me propose one thing that would
be maybe, maybe the only thing that makes

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:41.799
Mark Zuckerberg word salad answer a little
bit less disturbing.

00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:45.500
Trump often doesn't know what the hell he's
talking about and nobody around him does.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:51.690
Is it possible that the reason Mark Zuckerberg
struggled to say what was discussed is because

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:55.140
he didn't understand what on earth Donald
Trump was talking about?

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:59.440
Is that maybe why he was unable to answer
Gayle King's question?

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.440
I'm kidding.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.359
Sort of mostly, but who knows.

00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:08.390
My guess is that the topics from that meeting
will ultimately play a role in the 2020 election.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.780
There's too much at stake right now.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:15.880
The dynamics, the power dynamics of what a
platform like Facebook can do when it comes

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.800
to influencing elections by virtue of what
they do and don't allow.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:24.840
The stakes are extremely high and I would
be shocked if whatever was discussed between

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.260
Trump and Zuckerberg doesn't ultimately play
a role in the 2020 election.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.560
Let me know what you think was talked about.

